### Design Summary

| Milestone | Rule Type | Target (spawn-relative) | Distance | Facing | Rationale |
|-----------|-----------|------------------------|----------|--------|-----------|
| find_red_wool | position_near_with_facing | [-5, 1, 0] | ≤5 blocks | ±60° | Red wool pillar center in west room; player must enter room and look at it |
| find_brown_bed | position_near_with_facing | [7, 0, 0] | ≤5 blocks | ±60° | Brown bed foot in east room; player must enter room and look at it |

**Why these thresholds work:**
- The west room spans x=-10 to x=-3, so the red wool at x=-5 is ~2 blocks from the doorway. A player standing in the doorway at x=-3 is 2 blocks away — well within the 5-block max_distance.
- The east room spans x=4 to x=10, so the bed at x=7 is ~3 blocks from the doorway. A player in the doorway at x=4 is 3 blocks away — also within range.
- Both thresholds ensure the player has actually navigated to the correct room rather than triggering from the center room (center room to red wool = ~5 blocks, to bed = ~7 blocks, so the bed milestone cannot trigger from center).

